@comment openi2pd OpenBSD PLIST template; merge into the external port.
@comment Reserve _i2pd in infrastructure/db/user.list before merge; the number
@comment below is a template placeholder and must not collide with another port.
@newgroup _i2pd:838
@comment @newuser fields are name:uid:gid:class:change:expire:gecos:home:shell.
@comment The class `i2pd` is the login class that supplies the 8192 open-file
@comment limits and the 0077 mask; /sbin/nologin keeps the account out of any
@comment interactive login and the state directory stays private to it.
@newuser _i2pd:838:838:i2pd:0:0:i2pd account:/var/i2pd:/sbin/nologin
@rcscript ${RCDIR}/i2pd
@comment /var/i2pd is created from share/examples/var/i2pd and is private to
@comment the service account; the certificate tree stays read-only below
@comment /usr/local/share and is not a mutable sample.
@comment pkg/var-i2pd.README is therefore a package marker, not documentation
@comment that may be dropped: without a file in share/examples/var/i2pd the
@comment @sample below creates nothing.
share/examples/var/i2pd/README
@comment @mode/@owner/@group apply to every following entry until they are
@comment reset. This block creates the private state directory; the block after
@comment it additionally makes the subscription sample writable by the daemon.
@mode 0700
@owner _i2pd
@group _i2pd
@sample ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/i2pd/
@mode 0640
@owner _i2pd
@group _i2pd
share/examples/var/i2pd/subscriptions.txt
@sample ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/i2pd/subscriptions.txt
@mode
@owner
@group
@comment The reset above matters: the configuration and login-class samples are
@comment installed root-owned, so the daemon can read but never rewrite /etc.
@comment The man pages come from the CMake Runtime/Tui components and the
@comment desktop/icon files from the Tui component; the certificate tree below
@comment is package-owned read-only content, which is why no state or
@comment certificate sample is listed here.
